# StudyFlow AI — Comprehensive Project Report

Prepared for: Shubham Kumari (kumarishubham177@gmail.com)
Project: StudyFlow AI — AI-powered study material recommender and learning platform
Date: 21 September 2026

---

## 1. Executive Summary

StudyFlow AI is a full-stack learning platform that connects three kinds of people:

- **Students** — get personalised material recommendations, an AI tutor grounded in their own lecture notes, flashcard study packs, search, ratings and a learning history.
- **Educators / Teachers** — upload course material, tag topics, create and publish study packs, and track student progress.
- **Administrators** — review a submission queue, approve or reject materials with reasons, manage subjects and authors, and read analytics and feedback reports.

Everything runs on one codebase: a TanStack Start (React 19) front end, server functions running at the edge, and a PostgreSQL database with row-level security.

---

## 2. Architecture Overview

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  CLIENT  — React 19 + TanStack Router + Tailwind v4    │
│  routes/, components/study/, shadcn-ui                 │
└──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
                           │ typed RPC (createServerFn)
┌──────────────────────────▼─────────────────────────────┐
│  EDGE SERVER — TanStack Start server functions         │
│  Zod validation · Supabase auth middleware             │
│  Lovable AI Gateway (openai/gpt-6-astra)               │
└──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
                           │ SQL over HTTPS (RLS enforced)
┌──────────────────────────▼─────────────────────────────┐
│  DATABASE — PostgreSQL                                 │
│  tables + enums · RLS policies · SECURITY DEFINER fns  │
│  storage bucket: study-materials (private)             │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Three security layers:** the browser client never holds a privileged key; server functions verify the signed-in user; the database refuses any row the user is not allowed to see.

