## 6. Data Seeding

Seeding is **idempotent**: re-running the script never duplicates rows. The pattern is a `VALUES` CTE joined to `subjects` and `material_authors` by name, guarded by `WHERE NOT EXISTS`.

```sql
WITH new_materials (title, type, description, url, tags, topics,
                    approval_status, rejection_reason, subject_name, author_name) AS (
  VALUES
    ('Neural Networks and Deep Learning',
     'Article'::public.material_type,
     'Online textbook explaining backpropagation, convolutional layers and gradient descent.',
     'http://neuralnetworksanddeeplearning.com',
     ARRAY['deep-learning','neural-networks','math']::text[],
     ARRAY[]::text[],
     'approved'::public.material_approval_status, NULL,
     'Machine Learning', 'Andrew Ng')
    -- … 60+ further rows …
)
INSERT INTO public.materials
  (title, type, description, url, tags, topics,
   approval_status, rejection_reason, subject_id, author_id)
SELECT v.title, v.type, v.description, v.url, v.tags, v.topics,
       v.approval_status, v.rejection_reason, s.id, a.id
FROM new_materials v
JOIN public.subjects s            ON s.name = v.subject_name
LEFT JOIN public.material_authors a ON a.name = v.author_name
WHERE NOT EXISTS (
  SELECT 1 FROM public.materials m WHERE m.title = v.title
);
```

Key rules learned while seeding:

1. Cast enum literals explicitly (`'Article'::public.material_type`) and use only `PDF | Video | Article`.
2. The table is `public.materials`, **not** `public.study_materials`.
3. `material_authors` uses the column `biography`, not `bio`.
4. `study_packs` has no `level` column; flashcards use `question`, `answer`, `position`.

A `DO $$ … $$` block seeds the starter study pack "Neural network fundamentals" with eight flashcards, again only if it does not already exist.

**Current managed database contents:** 8 subjects, 12 authors, 94 materials (62 approved / 2 pending / 2 rejected among the original set), 2 study packs, 16 flashcards, 6 ratings.

