## 8. Sign-In — How It Works

`src/routes/login.tsx`:

```ts
const { error } = await supabase.auth.signInWithPassword({ email, password });
if (!error) await supabase.rpc('claim_primary_admin');
if (error) { toast.error(error.message); return; }
toast.success('Welcome back');
nav({ to: '/dashboard' });
```

Google sign-in:

```ts
const r = await lovable.auth.signInWithOAuth('google', {
  redirect_uri: window.location.origin,
});
```

The redirect target is the site origin, never a protected page — the session must hydrate before any guarded route loads.

Protected pages live under `src/routes/_authenticated/`, whose layout route redirects signed-out visitors to the login page before any data loader runs.

